-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- שם טוב — phase 9: 265 more names, compiled from a name-only list.
--
-- Run once in the Supabase SQL Editor, after phase 8.
--
-- The source for this batch was a bare list of 300 names (no metadata) —
-- 35 were repeats of the same name, leaving 265 unique. Every column below
-- (gender, meaning, origin flags, style, popularity, etc.) was compiled
-- name-by-name from real, well-established Hebrew/biblical name etymology,
-- the same standard used for the earlier catalogue batches. Two honest
-- notes on quality, matching the meaning_confidence column itself:
--
--   - A handful of names (e.g. מרים, אסתר, מרדכי) have real etymological
--     debate in the sources — those are marked 'uncertain', not 'verified',
--     rather than picking one theory and presenting it as settled.
--   - `origin` (the free-text display column) is left blank for this batch
--     — the boolean flags carry the real, structured signal, and guessing
--     a display string with more confidence than the data warrants seemed
--     worse than leaving it empty.
--
-- 167 of these 265 names already exist in the catalogue from earlier
-- batches; the upsert-by-text pattern (same as phases 5 and 7) updates
-- those in place rather than creating duplicates, so only 98 are genuinely
-- new rows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

